            "target_entity_type": "PhysicalScheme",
            "paragraph": "Historical meteorological time series of surrounding weather stations, operated by the German weather service (DWD), were interpolated to the patch centers. For future projections, results of climate models were interpolated to the same patches. The model computes all components of the soil water budget for each patch on a daily basis, including the seepage rate below the root zone, estimating actual evapotranspiration by a variant of the Penman-Monteith method (similar to Allen et al. 1998). Daily values of recharge are summed up to monthly values for calculation of the total recharge volume (see Eq. 2).",
            "ontology_conformed": false,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
