            "target_entity_instance": "southwest Germany",
            "target_entity_type": "No_Country_Region",
            "paragraph": "According to the ASG manager, severe water shortages have not occurred in the past. However, during the summer months, the extraction rates were often near their operational limits. Dry years had prolonged consequences on groundwater availability. This is evidenced by the years 2016 to 2020. After a dry winter 2016/17 groundwater storage sufficed to meet demands in 2017. High recharge rates in early 2018 secured the supply in this year, whereas the dry winter of 2018/2019 led to groundwater levels falling close to operational limits in the course of 2019 and required a reduction of extraction rates to avoid damage to the production wells (caused by water levels falling into the well-screen sections).",
